# SWHP Frontend Implementation Plan

This document outlines the detailed plan to develop the frontend for the Single Window Health Portal (SWHP) using a **feature-based architecture** powered by **Next.js (TypeScript)** and **Tailwind CSS**.

## 1. Frontend Architecture & Setup
- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router for native file-system routing).
- **Language:** TypeScript for static typing and enhanced developer experience.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS for responsive, modern, and dynamic design aesthetics.
- **State Management:** React Context API and local state hooks (no Redux).
- **HTTP Client:** Axios for API communication, configured with interceptors.
- **Directory Structure:** Feature-based slicing within the `src/` directory.

### Directory Structure (Feature-Based)
```text
src/
+-- app/             # Next.js App Router (Pages & Layouts)
¦   +-- login/page.tsx
¦   +-- register/page.tsx
¦   +-- apply/page.tsx
¦   +-- dashboard/page.tsx
¦   +-- layout.tsx
¦   +-- page.tsx
+-- components/      # Shared global components (Navbar, Footer)
+-- lib/             # Shared utilities, Axios instance setup
+-- features/        # Feature modules
¦   +-- auth/        # Login, Register, AccountMapping, AuthContext
¦   +-- profile/     # UserProfile form and state
¦   +-- services/    # Service Selection checklist and SWAN initialization
¦   +-- application/ # iFrame orchestrator, postMessage listener, progress tracker
¦   +-- payment/     # Fee aggregation UI, Gateway redirect logic
¦   +-- tracking/    # Unified tracking dashboard table
```

### Phase 1: Project Initialization & Routing
- [ ] Scaffold Next.js TypeScript application with Tailwind (`npx create-next-app@latest --ts --tailwind`).
- [ ] Install dependencies: `axios`, FontAwesome packages.
- [ ] Setup folder structure aligning with feature-based architecture (`src/features/...`).
- [ ] Implement `RootLayout` in `src/app/layout.tsx` integrating global Tailwind styles and AuthContext.

## 2. Core Features Implementation

### Phase 2: `features/auth` & `features/profile`
- [ ] **Auth Components:** Create visually stunning `Login`, `Register`, and `AccountMapping` components under `src/features/auth/components` utilizing Tailwind utility classes.
- [ ] **Auth Context:** Implement `AuthContext.tsx` in `src/features/auth/context` for JWT management.
- [ ] **Profile Management:** Create the `UserProfile` form under `src/features/profile/components`.

### Phase 3: `features/services` (Selection & SWAN)
- [ ] **Service Checklist:** Build `ServiceList.tsx` displaying available legacy services using modern card-based layouts styled with Tailwind.
- [ ] **SWAN Flow:** Create `hooks/useSwan.ts` inside `features/services` to call `/api/v1/swan/create`.

### Phase 4: `features/application` (iFrame Orchestration)
- [ ] **iFrame Container:** Create `ServiceIframe.tsx` in `features/application/components`.
- [ ] **postMessage Listener:** Implement `hooks/usePostMessage.ts` inside the application feature. Validate origins and payloads.
- [ ] **Queue Management:** Build `ApplicationOrchestrator.tsx` to advance through selected services with custom Tailwind progress indicators.

### Phase 5: `features/payment` & `features/tracking`
- [ ] **Payment UI:** Build `FeeSummary.tsx` in `features/payment/components` to fetch from `/api/v1/swan/{swan}/fees`.
- [ ] **Tracking Dashboard:** Build `TrackingTable.tsx` in `features/tracking/components` using styled responsive tables with Tailwind.

## 3. Security & Validation
- [ ] Apply **CAPTCHA** to auth forms.
- [ ] Implement **Strict Origin Validation** on all incoming `postMessage` events.
- [ ] Ensure **CSRF Protection** (handled via stateless JWT).
